        "original_id": "84b69af1-c352-5e59-ac06-b41d225c4808",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Movements: Mexican Indignados Movement\n- Conflicts: Mexican Drug War\n- Organizations: Mexican Government, drug trafficking syndicates\n- Topics: War on Drugs, corruption, economic inequality, poverty\n\nFacts:\n- The Mexican Indignados Movement, also called \"Movimiento por la Paz con Justicia y Dignidad,\" began on 28 March 2011 and is an ongoing protest movement.\n- The Mexican Indignados Movement began in response to the Mexican Drug War, government and corporate corruption, regressive economic policies, and growing economic inequality and poverty.\n- The Mexican Drug War, also called the Mexican War on Drugs, is the Mexican theater of the United States' War on Drugs.\n- The Mexican Drug War is an ongoing low-intensity asymmetric war between the Mexican Government and various drug trafficking syndicates.",
